Z||000000||Greg Piet||08-02-2000||02:29 AM||||OK I am confused.<BR>looking up compressors for my 2.8 in the pontiac manual it says I have a da-6 compressor.<P>checker auto online has 4 different compressors<BR>two are da6<BR>two are hr6<P>then there are two size pulleys 5.7" and 4.9" for each type of compressor<P>I want to use R134, so which compressor do I want???? <P>I am getting sick of driving around with the cabin temperature at 120+ with the windows open and the vista vent out!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phil||08-02-2000||07:19 AM||||I dragged the old one in with me. The compressor doesn't care what it compresses (R12 or 134A) but the the oil inside does. Just dump out whatever oil is in there and put in the proper type. You should replace your acc/dryer with one that is compatable with 134A also. Flush-new oriface tube and "O" rings- evacuate- fill-tada you're done.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||08-02-2000||08:03 AM||||My 85SE v-6 4spd has the DA-6 with I believe the smaller pulley.||||reg||1
